# Exact transitional compatibility baseline.
#
# Every entry identifies one currently detected implementation. The guard fails
# for both new detections and stale entries so deleting or renaming a function
# requires updating this file. Never add a directory or file wildcard: one
# existing exception must not exempt a new function in the same file.
#
# New archive readers belong in pkg/internal/archiveingest. New credential,
# header, body, URL, form, multipart, and auth policy belongs in
# pkg/convert/credentialpolicy or pkg/convert/requestimport.

# Which entries are justified, and which are not
#
# An entry here is not automatically residual work. Some of these are genuinely
# format-local -- a source format's own template grammar, or a lossy review-
# artifact sanitizer whose whole point is that it is NOT the shared projection.
# Blocks below that carry a rationale comment have been checked, and the reason
# they stay is recorded so it is not re-derived.
#
# Blocks with no rationale comment have NOT been individually triaged. They may
# be real duplication worth centralizing, or format-local for good reason; nobody
# has checked. Absence of a comment means unknown, not endorsed -- and equally,
# it is not licence to assume duplication. The OpenAPI block records what that
# assumption cost when it was tested.

archive:pkg/convert/bruno/bundle.go
# mergeEnterpriseArchiveZipWithSupplementalFiles must WRITE a zip and must keep
# each entry's original name, because ConvertZip strips the first path segment
# and rewriting names to the normalized form would silently move every nested
# file up one level. It applies the shared policy via
# archiveingest.ValidateFilePath instead of adopting the normalizing reader.
archive:pkg/api/handlers_import_enterprise.go

# pkg/convert/bruno/inspect.go
# Bruno's {{...}} template grammar, its secret-expression canonicalization, and
# the deferred-vs-governed distinction OpenCollection semantics require. This is
